# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Freshdesk Triage Agent (operations)

Watches Freshdesk tickets on `{{FRESHDESK_DOMAIN}}.freshdesk.com` and drafts
grounded replies as PRIVATE notes — a human sends every customer-facing
reply. Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Freshdesk automation rule ("Trigger Webhook" — unsigned; the URL secret IS the auth)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/freshdesk-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/freshdesk-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output |
|---|---|---|
| New ticket | `triage` | ONE private note (draft reply + category); GitHub issue only for real bugs |
| New public reply on a tracked ticket | `respond` | Updated private note — or silence when a human already handled it |

State lives on the orphan branch `freshdesk-agent-state` (`state/<ticket_id>.json`:
phase, last_conversation_id, issue_url). Every run re-fetches truth from
Freshdesk's API and diffs against it — webhook payloads are only doorbells.
Agent notes are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver counts only
PUBLIC conversations (the agent's own notes are private), with recency tracked
by the numeric conversation id. The requester's opening message is the
ticket's `description_text`, not a conversation — untracked tickets go to
triage regardless, so nothing is lost.

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Freshdesk Triage Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles recent open tickets + tracked ones; a ticket id processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `AI_MODEL` in `scripts/freshdesk-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{AI_MODEL}}`, brain `{{BRAIN_NAME}}`).
- **Pause:** disable the two automation rules (Admin → Workflows → Automations) — no code change needed.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs FRESHDESK_API_KEY exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/freshdesk-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<ticket_id> bash scripts/freshdesk-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Freshdesk writes are **private notes only** — `note.sh` hardcodes `private: true`, so the agent is structurally unable to reply to customers; a human sends every reply.
- Never changes ticket status, priority, or assignee — humans own the queue.
- Never escalates twice: the GitHub issue URL is saved in state (`issue_url`); follow-ups comment on that issue instead of opening a new one.
- No customer personal data (names, emails) in GitHub issues — describe, don't paste.
- Automation webhooks are unsigned — the relay authenticates by the secret URL path; rotate `WEBHOOK_SECRET` (and both rules' URLs) if it ever leaks.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
